        "title": "security: rebuild standalone binaries with Bun 1.4.4+ for Brotli CVE-2026-111497",
        "description": "## Problem The standalone gbrain executable embeds Bun 1.4.3, which contains the Brotli decoder flaw tracked as **CVE-2026-111497**. Bun has released **1.4.4** containing the fix, but gbrain's release workflow still specifies 1.4.3. This is a runtime/build dependency report for an already public vulnerability, not a claim of a newly discovered gbrain-specific exploit or an observed compromise. ## Observed evidence - On a macOS arm64 standalone installation, `gbrain --version` reports **0.60.360.0**. - `GBRAIN_SKIP_STARTUP_HOOKS=1 gbrain doctor --only bun_runtime --json` reports: ```json {\"name\":\"bun_runtime\",\"status\":\"ok\",\"message\":\"Bun 1.4.3 (minimum 1.4.0)\"} ``` This is the selected check object, with unrelated diagnostic fields omitted. The check is testing the supported version floor, not security currency. - Both `master` and `latest-stable` versions of [`.github/workflows/release.yml`](https://github.com/garrytan/gbrain/blob/master/.github/workflows/release.yml) still specify `bun-version: 1.4.3` at the time of reporting. - The package's standalone build uses `bun build --compile`, so updating the separately installed `bun` executable does not replace the runtime embedded in an existing gbrain binary. These are version/build-configuration observations. No malicious payload or exploit was executed, and no isolated gbrain exploit reproduction is claimed. ## Upstream security references - [Bun issue #46352](https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/issues/46352) describes the shared Brotli decoder flaw, including reachability through `fetch()` responses with `Content-Encoding: br` and decompression APIs. - [Bun merged fix #46392](https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/pull/46392) updates Brotli. The published `bun-v1.4.4` tag contains that merge.\n\n## Requested fix 1. Update the Bun toolchain used for standalone release builds to **1.4.4 or a newer fixed release**, covering every supported binary target. 2. Rebuild and publish the standalone binaries with the patched embedded runtime. 3. Document that existing standalone installations need the replacement gbrain executable and a restart of resident gbrain services; upgrading...
